{"content_hash": "f31f42eca6538746", "version_id": 452, "article_id": 46, "level_code": "en_a2", "lang": "en", "level": 2, "level_label": "A2 初级", "title": "Strong earthquake hits Panama and damages buildings", "title_zh": "巴拿马发生强震，多栋建筑受损", "has_translation": true, "topic": "world", "source": "bbc_world", "source_url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c620r39zdp9wo?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1677233860259-ce1a8e0f8498?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8MXx8cG93ZXJmdWwlMjBtYWduaXR1ZGUlMjBlYXJ0aHF1YWtlfGVufDB8MHx8fDE3OTE1OTQ2NTJ8MA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Çağlar Oskay on Unsplash", "author": "Çağlar Oskay", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@oskaycaglar?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/a-car-is-parked-in-front-of-a-destroyed-building-mmLtohu4qmE?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(73, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(111, 46%, 48%)", "label": "WORLD", "seed": "69c1918b4164"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-09", "word_count": 119, "reading_minutes": 0.6, "lead": "A big earthquake shook Panama on Friday. It damaged buildings and many people felt the strong shaking. No one has died, reports say.", "lead_zh": "周五，一场强烈地震袭击了巴拿马。地震损坏了建筑，很多人都感觉到了强烈震动。据报道，目前没有人死亡。", "preview": "The earthquake had a magnitude of 7.7. It happened just before 3pm local time. The centre was near a small town called Pitaloza Arriba. Abou", "preview_zh": "这次地震震级为7.7级，发生在当地时间下午3点前。震中位于一个叫皮塔洛萨阿里巴的小镇附近。大约460万人感觉到了震动。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 442, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/46/en_a2.mp3", "duration": 52.863, "size_bytes": 320976, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural", "word_count": 150, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@fc48a26/content/data/versions/452.json", "paragraphs": ["The earthquake had a magnitude of 7.7. It happened just before 3pm local time. The centre was near a small town called Pitaloza Arriba. About 4.6 million people felt the shaking.", "In the towns of Penonomé and Soná, some buildings fell down. Part of a cathedral in Penonomé broke, and a hotel almost fell down. In Panama City, about 200km away, people ran outside.", "President José Raúl Mulino said his government is working to help. Tsunami warnings went out for 11 countries, but later they were cancelled. The Panama Canal was not affected.", "A 74-year-old man in Herrera province said his house has cracks. \"We are scared,\" he said. The earthquake came three days before a national safety drill."], "paragraphs_zh": ["这次地震震级为7.7级，发生在当地时间下午3点前。震中位于一个叫皮塔洛萨阿里巴的小镇附近。大约460万人感觉到了震动。", "在佩诺诺梅和索纳等城镇，一些建筑倒塌了。佩诺诺梅一座大教堂的一部分被震坏，一家酒店几乎完全倒塌。在约200公里外的巴拿马城，人们纷纷跑到室外。", "总统何塞·劳尔·穆利诺表示，政府正在努力提供帮助。海啸警报曾对11个国家发布，但后来被取消。巴拿马运河没有受到影响。", "埃雷拉省一位74岁的男子说，他家的房子出现了裂缝。“我们很害怕，”他说。这次地震发生前三天，全国本来要举行一次安全演习。"], "body": "The earthquake had a magnitude of 7.7. It happened just before 3pm local time. The centre was near a small town called Pitaloza Arriba. About 4.6 million people felt the shaking.\n\nIn the towns of Penonomé and Soná, some buildings fell down. Part of a cathedral in Penonomé broke, and a hotel almost fell down. In Panama City, about 200km away, people ran outside.\n\nPresident José Raúl Mulino said his government is working to help. Tsunami warnings went out for 11 countries, but later they were cancelled. The Panama Canal was not affected.\n\nA 74-year-old man in Herrera province said his house has cracks. \"We are scared,\" he said. The earthquake came three days before a national safety drill.", "body_zh": "这次地震震级为7.7级，发生在当地时间下午3点前。震中位于一个叫皮塔洛萨阿里巴的小镇附近。大约460万人感觉到了震动。\n\n在佩诺诺梅和索纳等城镇，一些建筑倒塌了。佩诺诺梅一座大教堂的一部分被震坏，一家酒店几乎完全倒塌。在约200公里外的巴拿马城，人们纷纷跑到室外。\n\n总统何塞·劳尔·穆利诺表示，政府正在努力提供帮助。海啸警报曾对11个国家发布，但后来被取消。巴拿马运河没有受到影响。\n\n埃雷拉省一位74岁的男子说，他家的房子出现了裂缝。“我们很害怕，”他说。这次地震发生前三天，全国本来要举行一次安全演习。", "text": "The earthquake had a magnitude of 7.7. It happened just before 3pm local time. The centre was near a small town called Pitaloza Arriba. About 4.6 million people felt the shaking. In the towns of Penonomé and Soná, some buildings fell down. Part of a cathedral in Penonomé broke, and a hotel almost fell down. In Panama City, about 200km away, people ran outside. President José Raúl Mulino said his government is working to help. Tsunami warnings went out for 11 countries, but later they were cancelled. The Panama Canal was not affected. A 74-year-old man in Herrera province said his house has cracks. \"We are scared,\" he said. The earthquake came three days before a national safety drill.", "vocab": [{"word": "earthquake", "pos": "noun", "zh": "地震", "note": "常说 a big/small earthquake"}, {"word": "magnitude", "pos": "noun", "zh": "震级", "note": "地震强度，如 magnitude 7.7"}, {"word": "damage", "pos": "verb", "zh": "损坏", "note": "也可作名词：damage to buildings"}, {"word": "building", "pos": "noun", "zh": "建筑物，楼房", "note": ""}, {"word": "town", "pos": "noun", "zh": "城镇", "note": "比 city 小"}, {"word": "warning", "pos": "noun", "zh": "警报", "note": "如 tsunami warning 海啸警报"}, {"word": "scared", "pos": "adj", "zh": "害怕的", "note": "口语常用，= afraid"}, {"word": "drill", "pos": "noun", "zh": "演习，演练", "note": "如 a safety drill 安全演习"}], "title_original": "Powerful magnitude 7.7 earthquake hits Panama, damaging buildings", "summary_original": "Tsunami warnings are issued for neighbouring countries as videos of destruction circulate online.", "body_original": "Powerful magnitude 7.7 earthquake hits Panama, damaging buildings\nBy\nMichael Sheils McNamee\nPublished\n9 October 2026\nA massive magnitude 7.7 earthquake has hit Panama, damaging buildings and causing widespread shaking.\nAbout 4.6 million people felt moderate to severe tremors as a result of the quake, according to the US Geological Survey, which has said that the effects of the quake were \"likely to be widespread\".\nIt struck just before 15:00 local time (18:00 GMT) on Friday, with an epicentre about 6.2 miles (10km) from the town of Pitaloza Arriba in south-central Panama.\nFootage shared online appears to show collapsed buildings in the towns of Penonomé and Soná, including one of a man calling out to anyone trapped under the rubble of a collapsed building. No casualties have so far been reported.\nVerified footage shows one side of a cathedral in Penonomé collapsed due to the shaking, as well as one of its spires.\nAnother video showed a local hotel had almost completely collapsed.\nRicardo Brown, who lives in the southern Herrera province, told news agency Reuters that the earthquake had damaged several homes in his neighbourhood of Las Minas.\n\"We're scared. It's just the two of us old folks here. The house has cracked and we're afraid it could fall on us,\" the 74-year-old said.\nThe full extent of the damage it has caused is not yet clear, though several large aftershocks were also reported near the initial earthquake, potentially complicating the situation on the surface.\nThe quake was registered as occurring at a depth of just 12km. The shallower the earthquake, the more likely it is to have more severe effects on the surface.\nMany people were evacuated from buildings in Panama City, about 200km from the epicentre, and were seen taking to the streets or sitting in nearby parks until the shaking had ceased.\nDamage in the capital appears to be limited to that caused by debris falling from roofs.\nPanama's President José Raúl Mulino said his entire government was mobilising in response to the earthquake, adding: \"What happened should not be used to cause alarm or disorder.\"\nTsunami warnings were initially issued for 11 countries neighbouring Panama, before the US Tsunami Warning System confirmed there was no threat.\nThe Panama Canal - a vital waterway linking the Atlantic and Pacific oceans - was unaffected by the earthquake, the authority that oversees marine traffic through it said.\nThe earthquake comes just three days before Panama was scheduled to hold a national evacuation drill for dealing with a major earthquake.\nIt also follows devastating earthquakes in Colombia and Venezuela earlier this year.\nRelated topics\nMexico\nEarthquakes\nChile\nPanama", "fetched_at": "2026-10-10T01:10:50.719840", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "The", "s": 0.1, "e": 0.275, "sm": 100, "em": 275, "cs": 0, "ce": 3, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "earthquake", "s": 0.287, "e": 0.838, "sm": 287, "em": 837, "cs": 4, "ce": 14, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "had", "s": 0.85, "e": 1.0, "sm": 850, "em": 1000, "cs": 15, "ce": 18, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "a", "s": 1.012, "e": 1.052, "sm": 1012, "em": 1052, "cs": 19, "ce": 20, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": "magnitude", "s": 1.062, "e": 1.675, "sm": 1062, "em": 1675, "cs": 21, "ce": 30, "si": 0}, {"i": 5, "w": "of", "s": 1.688, "e": 1.775, "sm": 1687, "em": 1775, "cs": 31, "ce": 33, "si": 0}, {"i": 6, "w": "7.7", "s": 1.788, "e": 2.925, "sm": 1787, "em": 2925, "cs": 34, "ce": 37, "si": 0}, {"i": 7, "w": ".", "s": 2.925, "e": 3.8, "sm": 2925, "em": 3800, "cs": 37, "ce": 38, "si": 0}, {"i": 8, "w": "It", "s": 3.8, "e": 3.95, "sm": 3800, "em": 3949, "cs": 39, "ce": 41, "si": 1}, {"i": 9, "w": "happened", "s": 3.962, "e": 4.388, "sm": 3962, "em": 4387, "cs": 42, "ce": 50, "si": 1}, {"i": 10, "w": "just", "s": 4.4, "e": 4.65, "sm": 4400, "em": 4650, "cs": 51, "ce": 55, "si": 1}, {"i": 11, "w": "before", "s": 4.662, "e": 4.975, "sm": 4662, "em": 4975, "cs": 56, "ce": 62, "si": 1}, {"i": 12, "w": "3", "s": 4.987, "e": 5.196, "sm": 4987, "em": 5195, "cs": 63, "ce": 64, "si": 1}, {"i": 13, "w": "pm", "s": 5.196, "e": 5.612, "sm": 5195, "em": 5612, "cs": 64, "ce": 66, "si": 1}, {"i": 14, "w": "local", "s": 5.625, "e": 5.925, "sm": 5625, "em": 5925, "cs": 67, "ce": 72, "si": 1}, {"i": 15, "w": "time", "s": 5.938, "e": 6.4, "sm": 5937, "em": 6400, "cs": 73, "ce": 77, "si": 1}, {"i": 16, "w": ".", "s": 